@page "/pixata-grid"
@using Pixata.Blazor.Components
@using Pixata.Blazor.Components.Grid
@using Pixata.Blazor.Sample.Models
@using Pixata.Blazor.Sample.Data
@using Pixata.Extensions.Grid
@using Pixata.Blazor.Grid.Excel
@using ClosedXML.Excel
@using System.IO
@inject GridSampleEmployeeService EmployeeService
@using Pixata.Blazor.Extensions
@inject TemplateHelper TemplateHelper

<SitePageTitle>Pixata grid</SitePageTitle>

<h3>Pixata grid</h3>

<p><code>PixataGrid</code> is a data grid with paging, sorting, filtering, editing, grouping and much more. Each section below shows one of its features. See <a href="https://github.com/MrYossu/Pixata.Utilities/blob/master/Pixata.Blazor/Readme.Grid.md">the documentation</a>.</p>

<div class="pixata-blazor-grid-sample-options">
  <label>
    Size
    <select @bind="_size">
      @foreach (PixataGridSize size in Enum.GetValues<PixataGridSize>()) {
        <option value="@size">@size</option>
      }
    </select>
  </label>
  <label>
    <input type="checkbox" @bind="_empty" />
    No data
  </label>
</div>

<h4>Declared columns</h4>

<p>The First name column has a width, Date of birth gets its format from a <code>[DisplayFormat]</code> attribute, Salary has a <code>DisplayFormat</code> and is right-aligned, and City is a nested field (<code>Address.City</code>). Columns without a <code>Title</code> get one from a <code>[Display(Name)]</code> attribute, or else from the field name split into words (so <code>DateOfBirth</code> becomes "Date of birth").</p>

<PixataGrid Data="Data" Size="_size" Height="300px">
  <GridColumns>
    <PixataGridColumn Field="@nameof(GridSampleEmployee.FirstName)" Width="140px" />
    <PixataGridColumn Field="@nameof(GridSampleEmployee.Surname)" />
    <PixataGridColumn Field="@nameof(GridSampleEmployee.Email)" />
    <PixataGridColumn Field="@nameof(GridSampleEmployee.DateOfBirth)" />
    <PixataGridColumn Field="@nameof(GridSampleEmployee.Salary)" DisplayFormat="{0:C2}" TextAlign="PixataGridTextAlign.Right" />
    <PixataGridColumn Field="Address.City" Title="City" />
  </GridColumns>
</PixataGrid>

<h4>Paging</h4>

<p>The grid's <code>Page</code> and <code>PageSize</code> are bound, so the page knows where it is. The pager shows 5 page buttons at a time, and offers page sizes of 3, 5, 10 and All. Narrow the window to see the pager adapt.</p>

<div class="pixata-blazor-grid-sample-options">
  <label>
    Pager input
    <select @bind="_pagerInputType">
      @foreach (PixataGridPagerInputType inputType in Enum.GetValues<PixataGridPagerInputType>()) {
        <option value="@inputType">@inputType</option>
      }
    </select>
  </label>
  <label>
    Pager position
    <select @bind="_pagerPosition">
      @foreach (PixataGridPagerPosition position in Enum.GetValues<PixataGridPagerPosition>()) {
        <option value="@position">@position</option>
      }
    </select>
  </label>
  <span>Page @_page, page size @_pageSize</span>
</div>

<PixataGrid Data="Data" Size="_size" Pageable="true" @bind-PageSize="_pageSize" @bind-Page="_page">
  <GridSettings>
    <PixataGridPagerSettings ButtonCount="5" PageSizes="@_pageSizes" InputType="_pagerInputType" Position="_pagerPosition" />
  </GridSettings>
  <GridColumns>
    <PixataGridColumn Field="@nameof(GridSampleEmployee.FirstName)" />
    <PixataGridColumn Field="@nameof(GridSampleEmployee.Surname)" />
    <PixataGridColumn Field="@nameof(GridSampleEmployee.Email)" />
  </GridColumns>
</PixataGrid>

<h4>Sorting</h4>

<p>Click a header to sort by that column. Clicking again sorts the other way, and a third click removes the sort. In multiple mode, each click adds to the sort, and the header shows the order. City is a nested field.</p>

<div class="pixata-blazor-grid-sample-options">
  <label>
    <input type="checkbox" @bind="_multipleSort" />
    Sort by several columns
  </label>
</div>

<PixataGrid Data="Data" Size="_size" Sortable="true" SortMode="@(_multipleSort ? PixataGridSortMode.Multiple : PixataGridSortMode.Single)" Pageable="true" PageSize="5">
  <GridColumns>
    <PixataGridColumn Field="@nameof(GridSampleEmployee.FirstName)" />
    <PixataGridColumn Field="@nameof(GridSampleEmployee.Surname)" />
    <PixataGridColumn Field="@nameof(GridSampleEmployee.DateOfBirth)" />
    <PixataGridColumn Field="@nameof(GridSampleEmployee.Salary)" DisplayFormat="{0:C2}" TextAlign="PixataGridTextAlign.Right" />
    <PixataGridColumn Field="@nameof(GridSampleEmployee.IsManager)" Sortable="false" Title="Manager (not sortable)" />
    <PixataGridColumn Field="Address.City" Title="City" />
  </GridColumns>
</PixataGrid>

<h4>Filtering</h4>

<div class="pixata-blazor-grid-sample-options">
  <label>
    Filter mode
    <select @bind="_filterMode">
      <option value="row">Filter row</option>
      <option value="menu">Filter menu</option>
      <option value="checkbox">Filter menu with checkbox lists</option>
    </select>
  </label>
</div>

<p>Try the filter row, the filter menus and the search box (which searches the text columns). City can't be filtered, but it can be searched.</p>

<PixataGrid Data="Data" Size="_size" FilterMode="@(_filterMode == "row" ? PixataGridFilterMode.FilterRow : PixataGridFilterMode.FilterMenu)" Pageable="true" PageSize="5" Sortable="true">
  <GridToolBarTemplate>
    <PixataGridSearchBox />
  </GridToolBarTemplate>
  <GridColumns>
    <PixataGridColumn Field="@nameof(GridSampleEmployee.FirstName)" FilterMenuType="@PixataFilterMenuType" />
    <PixataGridColumn Field="@nameof(GridSampleEmployee.DateOfBirth)" FilterMenuType="@PixataFilterMenuType" />
    <PixataGridColumn Field="@nameof(GridSampleEmployee.Salary)" DisplayFormat="{0:C2}" FilterMenuType="@PixataFilterMenuType" />
    <PixataGridColumn Field="@nameof(GridSampleEmployee.IsManager)" FilterMenuType="@PixataFilterMenuType" />
    <PixataGridColumn Field="@nameof(GridSampleEmployee.Pet)" FilterMenuType="@PixataFilterMenuType" />
    <PixataGridColumn Field="Address.City" Title="City" Filterable="false" />
  </GridColumns>
</PixataGrid>

<h4>Supplying the data with OnRead</h4>

<p>This grid gets its data from the sample app's database through <code>OnRead</code>, so only the page being shown is loaded. Each read is slowed down to 1.5 seconds, so you can see the loading indicator when you page, sort or filter (it isn't shown for the first read). It uses <code>ToGridResultAsync()</code> from Pixata.AspNetCore, which runs the paging, sorting and filtering in the database.</p>

<PixataGrid TItem="GridSampleEmployee" OnRead="ReadEmployees" Size="_size" Pageable="true" PageSize="5" Sortable="true" FilterMode="PixataGridFilterMode.FilterRow">
  <GridColumns>
    <PixataGridColumn Field="@nameof(GridSampleEmployee.FirstName)" />
    <PixataGridColumn Field="@nameof(GridSampleEmployee.Surname)" />
    <PixataGridColumn Field="@nameof(GridSampleEmployee.Salary)" DisplayFormat="{0:C2}" />
    <PixataGridColumn Field="Address.City" Title="City" />
  </GridColumns>
</PixataGrid>

<h4>Templates and row events</h4>

<p>The name is a template, the salary header has a template, managers' rows get a CSS class from <code>OnRowRender</code>, and salaries over 300,000 get one from <code>OnCellRender</code>. Click a row to see <code>OnRowClick</code>, or right-click it for <code>OnRowContextMenu</code>.</p>

<p>@_rowEvent</p>

<PixataGrid TItem="GridSampleEmployee" Data="Data" Size="_size" Pageable="true" PageSize="5"
            OnRowRender="PixataRowRender"
            OnRowClick="RowClicked"
            OnRowContextMenu="RowRightClicked">
  <GridColumns>
    <PixataGridColumn Title="Name">
      <Template>
        <strong>@((context as GridSampleEmployee)!.FirstName)</strong> @((context as GridSampleEmployee)!.Surname)
      </Template>
    </PixataGridColumn>
    <PixataGridColumn TItem="GridSampleEmployee" Field="@nameof(GridSampleEmployee.Salary)" DisplayFormat="{0:C2}" OnCellRender="PixataSalaryRender">
      <HeaderTemplate>
        Salary <em>(GBP)</em>
      </HeaderTemplate>
    </PixataGridColumn>
    <PixataGridColumn Field="@nameof(GridSampleEmployee.IsManager)" Title="Manager" />
  </GridColumns>
</PixataGrid>

<h4>Templates from the TemplateHelper</h4>

<p>A column's <code>Template</code> can be built with the <a href="https://github.com/MrYossu/Pixata.Utilities/blob/master/Pixata.Blazor/Readme.Helpers.md#templatehelper"><code>TemplateHelper</code></a>, which saves writing the markup and casting the context. The email is a link, and the salary is right-aligned, in red if it's over 300,000.</p>

<PixataGrid TItem="GridSampleEmployee" Data="Data" Size="_size" Pageable="true" PageSize="5">
  <GridColumns>
    <PixataGridColumn Field="@nameof(GridSampleEmployee.FirstName)" />
    <PixataGridColumn Field="@nameof(GridSampleEmployee.Surname)" />
    <PixataGridColumn Field="@nameof(GridSampleEmployee.Email)"
                      Template="@(TemplateHelper.Link<GridSampleEmployee>(e => e.Email, e => $"mailto:{e.Email}", title: "Send an email"))" />
    <PixataGridColumn Field="@nameof(GridSampleEmployee.Salary)"
                      Template="@(TemplateHelper.Text<GridSampleEmployee>(e => e.Salary.ToString("C0"), e => e.Salary > 300000 ? "text-align: right; color: red" : "text-align: right"))" />
  </GridColumns>
</PixataGrid>

<p>Inject the helper (or inherit <code>CommonComponentBase&lt;T&gt;</code>, which does it for you), and pass what it builds to the column's <code>Template</code>...</p>

<pre class="export-comparison">@TemplateHelperCode</pre>

<h4>Selection</h4>

<p>Click a row to select it, Ctrl+click to add or remove one, and Shift+click to select a range, or press on a row and drag. The checkbox column selects rows too, and its header selects all the rows on the page. The selection is kept as you move between pages.</p>

<PixataGrid Data="Data" Size="_size" Pageable="true" PageSize="5" SelectionMode="PixataGridSelectionMode.Multiple" @bind-SelectedItems="_pixataSelected">
  <GridColumns>
    <PixataGridCheckboxColumn />
    <PixataGridColumn Field="@nameof(GridSampleEmployee.FirstName)" />
    <PixataGridColumn Field="@nameof(GridSampleEmployee.Surname)" />
    <PixataGridColumn Field="@nameof(GridSampleEmployee.Salary)" DisplayFormat="{0:C2}" />
  </GridColumns>
</PixataGrid>
<p>Selected: @string.Join(", ", _pixataSelected.Select(e => e.FirstName))</p>

<p>With <code>SelectionType</code> set to <code>Cell</code>, the user selects cells instead, by clicking (with Ctrl and Shift as for rows) or by dragging out a rectangle.</p>

<PixataGrid Data="Data" Size="_size" Pageable="true" PageSize="5" SelectionMode="PixataGridSelectionMode.Multiple" @bind-SelectedCells="_selectedCells">
  <GridSettings>
    <PixataGridSelectionSettings SelectionType="PixataGridSelectionType.Cell" />
  </GridSettings>
  <GridColumns>
    <PixataGridColumn Field="@nameof(GridSampleEmployee.FirstName)" />
    <PixataGridColumn Field="@nameof(GridSampleEmployee.Surname)" />
    <PixataGridColumn Field="@nameof(GridSampleEmployee.Salary)" DisplayFormat="{0:C2}" />
  </GridColumns>
</PixataGrid>
<p>Selected cells: @string.Join(", ", _selectedCells.Select(c => $"{c.DataItem.FirstName}'s {c.ColumnField}"))</p>

<h4>Editing</h4>

<div class="pixata-blazor-grid-sample-options">
  <label>
    Edit mode
    <select @bind="_editMode">
      <option value="inline">Inline</option>
      <option value="popup">Popup</option>
      <option value="incell">In cell</option>
    </select>
  </label>
</div>

<p>The grid edits its own copy of the first 12 employees. First name is required (try saving without one), and the email address can't be changed.</p>

<PixataGrid TItem="GridSampleEditableEmployee" Data="_pixataEditable" Size="_size" Pageable="true" PageSize="5" ConfirmDelete="true"
            EditMode="@PixataEditMode"
            OnCreate="PixataCreate" OnUpdate="PixataUpdate" OnDelete="PixataDelete">
  <GridToolBarTemplate>
    <PixataGridCommandButton Command="Add" Icon="PixataGridIcon.Plus">Add employee</PixataGridCommandButton>
  </GridToolBarTemplate>
  <GridColumns>
    <PixataGridColumn Field="@nameof(GridSampleEditableEmployee.FirstName)" />
    <PixataGridColumn Field="@nameof(GridSampleEditableEmployee.Surname)" />
    <PixataGridColumn Field="@nameof(GridSampleEditableEmployee.Email)" Editable="false" />
    <PixataGridColumn Field="@nameof(GridSampleEditableEmployee.DateOfBirth)" DisplayFormat="{0:dd MMM yyyy}" />
    <PixataGridColumn Field="@nameof(GridSampleEditableEmployee.Salary)" DisplayFormat="{0:C2}" />
    <PixataGridColumn Field="@nameof(GridSampleEditableEmployee.IsManager)" />
    <PixataGridColumn Field="@nameof(GridSampleEditableEmployee.Pet)" />
    <PixataGridCommandColumn Width="180px">
      <PixataGridCommandButton Command="Edit" Icon="PixataGridIcon.Pencil">Edit</PixataGridCommandButton>
      <PixataGridCommandButton Command="Delete" Icon="PixataGridIcon.Trash">Delete</PixataGridCommandButton>
      <PixataGridCommandButton Command="Save" Icon="PixataGridIcon.Save" ShowInEdit="true">Save</PixataGridCommandButton>
      <PixataGridCommandButton Command="Cancel" Icon="PixataGridIcon.Cancel" ShowInEdit="true">Cancel</PixataGridCommandButton>
    </PixataGridCommandColumn>
  </GridColumns>
</PixataGrid>

<h4>Grouping and aggregates</h4>

<p>Drag a column header into the panel above the grid to group by it. The salary column has aggregates, shown in group footers and the grid's footer.</p>

<PixataGrid @ref="_groupedGrid" Data="Data" Size="_size" Groupable="true" Pageable="true" PageSize="8">
  <GridAggregates>
    <PixataGridAggregate Field="@nameof(GridSampleEmployee.Salary)" Aggregate="@Pixata.Extensions.Grid.GridAggregateType.Sum" />
    <PixataGridAggregate Field="@nameof(GridSampleEmployee.Salary)" Aggregate="@Pixata.Extensions.Grid.GridAggregateType.Average" />
    <PixataGridAggregate Field="@nameof(GridSampleEmployee.FirstName)" Aggregate="@Pixata.Extensions.Grid.GridAggregateType.Count" />
  </GridAggregates>
  <GridColumns>
    <PixataGridColumn Field="@nameof(GridSampleEmployee.FirstName)">
      <FooterTemplate>Total: @context.Count</FooterTemplate>
    </PixataGridColumn>
    <PixataGridColumn Field="@nameof(GridSampleEmployee.Surname)" />
    <PixataGridColumn Field="@nameof(GridSampleEmployee.Pet)" />
    <PixataGridColumn Field="@nameof(GridSampleEmployee.IsManager)" />
    <PixataGridColumn Field="@nameof(GridSampleEmployee.Salary)" DisplayFormat="{0:C0}">
      <GroupFooterTemplate>Sum: @(((decimal?)context.Sum)?.ToString("C0"))</GroupFooterTemplate>
      <FooterTemplate>Average: @(((decimal?)context.Average)?.ToString("C0"))</FooterTemplate>
    </PixataGridColumn>
  </GridColumns>
</PixataGrid>

<h4>Resizing and reordering columns</h4>

<p>Drag the edge of a header to resize its column, or double-click the edge to fit the column to its content. Drag a header onto another to move it. First name can't be made narrower than 80px, and salary can't be wider than 200px. Email can't be resized, and date of birth can't be moved.</p>

<PixataGrid Data="Data" Size="_size" Resizable="true" Reorderable="true" Pageable="true" PageSize="5" OnColumnResize="@((PixataGridColumnResizeEventArgs<GridSampleEmployee> args) => _columnEvent = $"{args.Column.HeaderText} resized to {args.Width}px")" OnColumnReorder="@((PixataGridColumnReorderEventArgs<GridSampleEmployee> args) => _columnEvent = $"{args.Column.HeaderText} moved from {args.OldIndex} to {args.NewIndex}")">
  <GridColumns>
    <PixataGridColumn Field="@nameof(GridSampleEmployee.FirstName)" Width="150px" MinResizableWidth="80" Id="first" />
    <PixataGridColumn Field="@nameof(GridSampleEmployee.Surname)" Width="150px" Id="surname" />
    <PixataGridColumn Field="@nameof(GridSampleEmployee.Email)" Resizable="false" Id="email" />
    <PixataGridColumn Field="@nameof(GridSampleEmployee.DateOfBirth)" DisplayFormat="{0:dd MMM yyyy}" Reorderable="false" Id="dob" />
    <PixataGridColumn Field="@nameof(GridSampleEmployee.Salary)" DisplayFormat="{0:C0}" MaxResizableWidth="200" Id="salary" />
  </GridColumns>
</PixataGrid>
<p>@_columnEvent</p>

<h4>Frozen columns</h4>

<p>The grid is narrower than its columns, so it scrolls sideways. Id and first name are frozen on the left, salary on the right, and pet, in the middle, sticks to the left once it gets there.</p>

<PixataGrid Data="Data" Size="_size" Width="800px" Height="300px">
  <GridColumns>
    <PixataGridColumn Field="@nameof(GridSampleEmployee.Id)" Width="80px" Locked="true" />
    <PixataGridColumn Field="@nameof(GridSampleEmployee.FirstName)" Width="150px" Locked="true" />
    <PixataGridColumn Field="@nameof(GridSampleEmployee.Surname)" Width="200px" />
    <PixataGridColumn Field="@nameof(GridSampleEmployee.Email)" Width="300px" />
    <PixataGridColumn Field="@nameof(GridSampleEmployee.Pet)" Width="120px" Locked="true" />
    <PixataGridColumn Field="@nameof(GridSampleEmployee.DateOfBirth)" Width="200px" DisplayFormat="{0:dd MMM yyyy}" />
    <PixataGridColumn Field="Address.City" Width="200px" />
    <PixataGridColumn Field="@nameof(GridSampleEmployee.Salary)" Width="150px" DisplayFormat="{0:C0}" Locked="true" />
  </GridColumns>
</PixataGrid>

<h4>Multi-column headers</h4>

<p>A column can contain other columns, which share a header above their own.</p>

<PixataGrid Data="Data" Size="_size" Sortable="true" Pageable="true" PageSize="5">
  <GridColumns>
    <PixataGridColumn Field="@nameof(GridSampleEmployee.Id)" Width="80px" />
    <PixataGridColumn Title="Name">
      <Columns>
        <PixataGridColumn Field="@nameof(GridSampleEmployee.FirstName)" />
        <PixataGridColumn Field="@nameof(GridSampleEmployee.Surname)" />
      </Columns>
    </PixataGridColumn>
    <PixataGridColumn Title="Details">
      <Columns>
        <PixataGridColumn Field="@nameof(GridSampleEmployee.Email)" />
        <PixataGridColumn Title="Other">
          <Columns>
            <PixataGridColumn Field="@nameof(GridSampleEmployee.Pet)" />
            <PixataGridColumn Field="@nameof(GridSampleEmployee.IsManager)" />
          </Columns>
        </PixataGridColumn>
      </Columns>
    </PixataGridColumn>
    <PixataGridColumn Field="@nameof(GridSampleEmployee.Salary)" DisplayFormat="{0:C0}" />
  </GridColumns>
</PixataGrid>

<h4>Column menu</h4>

<p>Each header has a menu for sorting, filtering, showing and hiding columns, freezing, grouping and moving. Email isn't in the column chooser, and pet has no menu.</p>

<PixataGrid Data="Data" Size="_size" ShowColumnMenu="true" Sortable="true" FilterMode="PixataGridFilterMode.FilterMenu" Groupable="true" Reorderable="true" Resizable="true" Pageable="true" PageSize="5">
  <GridSettings>
    <PixataGridColumnMenuSettings Lockable="true" Groupable="true" Reorderable="true" />
  </GridSettings>
  <GridColumns>
    <PixataGridColumn Field="@nameof(GridSampleEmployee.FirstName)" Width="150px" />
    <PixataGridColumn Field="@nameof(GridSampleEmployee.Surname)" Width="150px" />
    <PixataGridColumn Field="@nameof(GridSampleEmployee.Email)" Width="250px" VisibleInColumnChooser="false" />
    <PixataGridColumn Field="@nameof(GridSampleEmployee.Pet)" Width="120px" ShowColumnMenu="false" />
    <PixataGridColumn Field="@nameof(GridSampleEmployee.Salary)" Width="150px" DisplayFormat="{0:C0}" />
  </GridColumns>
</PixataGrid>

<h4>State</h4>

<p>Sort, filter, group, page, resize or move columns, then click Save. Change things again, and Restore puts them back. Reset goes back to how the grid started. The line under the grid shows the last change reported by <code>OnStateChanged</code>.</p>

<div class="pixata-blazor-grid-sample-options">
  <button type="button" class="pixata-btn pixata-btn-primary" @onclick="() => _pixataSavedState = _stateGrid!.GetState()">Save</button>
  <button type="button" class="pixata-btn pixata-btn-secondary" @onclick="() => _stateGrid!.SetState(_pixataSavedState)" disabled="@(_pixataSavedState is null)">Restore</button>
  <button type="button" class="pixata-btn pixata-btn-secondary" @onclick="() => _stateGrid!.SetState(null)">Reset</button>
</div>
<PixataGrid @ref="_stateGrid" Data="Data" Size="_size" Sortable="true" FilterMode="PixataGridFilterMode.FilterRow" Groupable="true" Resizable="true" Reorderable="true" Pageable="true" PageSize="5"
            OnStateChanged="@((PixataGridStateEventArgs<GridSampleEmployee> args) => _pixataStateChange = args.PropertyName ?? "")">
  <GridColumns>
    <PixataGridColumn Field="@nameof(GridSampleEmployee.FirstName)" />
    <PixataGridColumn Field="@nameof(GridSampleEmployee.Surname)" />
    <PixataGridColumn Field="@nameof(GridSampleEmployee.Pet)" />
    <PixataGridColumn Field="@nameof(GridSampleEmployee.Salary)" DisplayFormat="{0:C0}" />
  </GridColumns>
</PixataGrid>
<p>Last change: @_pixataStateChange</p>

<h4>Saving the state in local storage</h4>

<p>This grid has a <code>StorageKey</code>, so its state is saved in the browser's local storage whenever it changes. Change it, then refresh the page.</p>

<PixataGrid Data="Data" Size="_size" StorageKey="pixata-grid-sample-state" Sortable="true" FilterMode="PixataGridFilterMode.FilterRow" Groupable="true" Resizable="true" Reorderable="true" Pageable="true" PageSize="5">
  <GridToolBarTemplate>
    <PixataGridSearchBox />
  </GridToolBarTemplate>
  <GridColumns>
    <PixataGridColumn Field="@nameof(GridSampleEmployee.FirstName)" />
    <PixataGridColumn Field="@nameof(GridSampleEmployee.Surname)" />
    <PixataGridColumn Field="@nameof(GridSampleEmployee.Pet)" />
    <PixataGridColumn Field="@nameof(GridSampleEmployee.DateOfBirth)" DisplayFormat="{0:dd MMM yyyy}" />
    <PixataGridColumn Field="@nameof(GridSampleEmployee.Salary)" DisplayFormat="{0:C0}" />
  </GridColumns>
</PixataGrid>

<h4>Virtual scrolling</h4>

<p>With <code>ScrollMode="Virtual"</code>, only the rows in view (plus a few) are rendered, and more are rendered as you scroll, rather than paging. The second grid gets its rows through <code>OnRead</code>, slowed down to half a second, so placeholder rows show while they load.</p>

<PixataGrid Data="Data" Size="_size" ScrollMode="PixataGridScrollMode.Virtual" Height="400px" RowHeight="36" PageSize="20" Sortable="true" FilterMode="PixataGridFilterMode.FilterRow">
  <GridColumns>
    <PixataGridColumn Field="@nameof(GridSampleEmployee.Id)" Width="80px" />
    <PixataGridColumn Field="@nameof(GridSampleEmployee.FirstName)" />
    <PixataGridColumn Field="@nameof(GridSampleEmployee.Surname)" />
    <PixataGridColumn Field="@nameof(GridSampleEmployee.Pet)" />
    <PixataGridColumn Field="@nameof(GridSampleEmployee.Salary)" DisplayFormat="{0:C0}" />
  </GridColumns>
</PixataGrid>

<p class="pixata-blazor-grid-sample-label">With OnRead</p>
<PixataGrid TItem="GridSampleEmployee" OnRead="ReadEmployeesVirtually" Size="_size" ScrollMode="PixataGridScrollMode.Virtual" Height="400px" RowHeight="36" PageSize="20" Sortable="true">
  <GridColumns>
    <PixataGridColumn Field="@nameof(GridSampleEmployee.Id)" Width="80px" />
    <PixataGridColumn Field="@nameof(GridSampleEmployee.FirstName)" />
    <PixataGridColumn Field="@nameof(GridSampleEmployee.Surname)" />
    <PixataGridColumn Field="@nameof(GridSampleEmployee.Salary)" DisplayFormat="{0:C0}" />
  </GridColumns>
</PixataGrid>

<h4>Virtual columns</h4>

<p>With <code>ColumnVirtualization="true"</code>, only the columns in view are rendered. Every column needs a width. This grid has 30 columns.</p>

<PixataGrid Data="Data" Size="_size" ColumnVirtualization="true" ScrollMode="PixataGridScrollMode.Virtual" Height="300px" RowHeight="36" PageSize="20" Width="800px">
  <GridColumns>
    @foreach ((string field, string title) in WideColumns) {
      <PixataGridColumn Field="@field" Title="@title" Width="150px" />
    }
  </GridColumns>
</PixataGrid>

<h4>Detail rows</h4>

<p>Click the arrow at the start of a row to show its details, which here include another grid of the employees with the same pet. The line under the grid counts the rows expanded and collapsed.</p>

<PixataGrid Data="Data" Size="_size" Pageable="true" PageSize="5"
            OnRowExpand="@((PixataGridRowExpandEventArgs<GridSampleEmployee> args) => _pixataExpands++)" OnRowCollapse="@((PixataGridRowCollapseEventArgs<GridSampleEmployee> args) => _pixataCollapses++)">
  <DetailTemplate>
    <p><strong>@context.FirstName @context.Surname</strong>, @context.Email, born @context.DateOfBirth.ToString("d MMMM yyyy"), lives in @context.Address.City</p>
    <PixataGrid Data="@(Data.Where(e => e.Pet == context.Pet && e.Id != context.Id).Take(3))" Size="_size">
      <GridColumns>
        <PixataGridColumn Field="@nameof(GridSampleEmployee.FirstName)" />
        <PixataGridColumn Field="@nameof(GridSampleEmployee.Surname)" />
        <PixataGridColumn Field="@nameof(GridSampleEmployee.Pet)" />
      </GridColumns>
    </PixataGrid>
  </DetailTemplate>
  <GridColumns>
    <PixataGridColumn Field="@nameof(GridSampleEmployee.FirstName)" />
    <PixataGridColumn Field="@nameof(GridSampleEmployee.Surname)" />
    <PixataGridColumn Field="@nameof(GridSampleEmployee.Pet)" />
    <PixataGridColumn Field="@nameof(GridSampleEmployee.Salary)" DisplayFormat="{0:C0}" />
  </GridColumns>
</PixataGrid>
<p>Expanded @_pixataExpands times, collapsed @_pixataCollapses times</p>

<h4>Dragging rows</h4>

<p>Drag a row by its handle to move it within its grid, or into the other grid.</p>

<div class="pixata-blazor-grid-sample-pair">
  <PixataGrid @ref="_pixataDragLeft" Data="_pixataLeft" Size="_size" RowDraggable="true" SelectionMode="PixataGridSelectionMode.Multiple"
              OnRowDrop="@((PixataGridRowDropEventArgs<GridSampleEmployee> args) => PixataRowDrop(args, _pixataLeft))">
    <GridColumns>
      <PixataGridColumn Field="@nameof(GridSampleEmployee.FirstName)" />
      <PixataGridColumn Field="@nameof(GridSampleEmployee.Surname)" />
    </GridColumns>
  </PixataGrid>
  <PixataGrid @ref="_pixataDragRight" Data="_pixataRight" Size="_size" RowDraggable="true" SelectionMode="PixataGridSelectionMode.Multiple"
              OnRowDrop="@((PixataGridRowDropEventArgs<GridSampleEmployee> args) => PixataRowDrop(args, _pixataRight))">
    <GridColumns>
      <PixataGridColumn Field="@nameof(GridSampleEmployee.FirstName)" />
      <PixataGridColumn Field="@nameof(GridSampleEmployee.Surname)" />
    </GridColumns>
  </PixataGrid>
</div>

<h4>Export</h4>

<p>The toolbar buttons save the grid as a CSV or Excel file. The checkbox exports every row rather than just the page. The button under the grid shows what it exports.</p>

<div class="pixata-blazor-grid-sample-options">
  <label><input type="checkbox" @bind="_exportAllPages" /> Export all pages</label>
</div>

<PixataGrid @ref="_exportGrid" Data="Data" Size="_size" Pageable="true" PageSize="5" Sortable="true">
  <GridToolBarTemplate>
    <PixataGridCommandButton Command="CsvExport" Icon="PixataGridIcon.FileCsv">Export to CSV</PixataGridCommandButton>
    <PixataGridCommandButton Command="ExcelExport" Icon="PixataGridIcon.FileExcel">Export to Excel</PixataGridCommandButton>
  </GridToolBarTemplate>
  <GridExport>
    <PixataGridCsvExport FileName="pixata-grid-export" AllPages="_exportAllPages" />
    <PixataGridExcelExport FileName="pixata-grid-export" AllPages="_exportAllPages" />
  </GridExport>
  <GridColumns>
    <PixataGridColumn Field="@nameof(GridSampleEmployee.Id)" Width="80px" />
    <PixataGridColumn Field="@nameof(GridSampleEmployee.FirstName)" Width="150px" />
    <PixataGridColumn Field="@nameof(GridSampleEmployee.Surname)" />
    <PixataGridColumn Field="@nameof(GridSampleEmployee.DateOfBirth)" DisplayFormat="{0:dd MMM yyyy}" />
    <PixataGridColumn Field="@nameof(GridSampleEmployee.Salary)" DisplayFormat="{0:C0}" />
    <PixataGridColumn Field="@nameof(GridSampleEmployee.IsManager)" />
    <PixataGridColumn Field="@nameof(GridSampleEmployee.Pet)" />
  </GridColumns>
</PixataGrid>

<div class="pixata-blazor-grid-sample-options">
  <button type="button" class="pixata-btn pixata-btn-secondary" @onclick="ShowExports">Show what's exported</button>
</div>
@if (_exports is not null) {
  <pre class="export-comparison">@_exports</pre>
}

<h4>Keyboard navigation</h4>

<p>With <code>Navigable="true"</code>, the grid is a single tab stop. Tab into it, then use the arrow keys, Home and End (with Ctrl for the first and last cells), Page Up and Page Down to page, Enter on a header to sort, Space to select a row, and Alt+Down on a header to open its menu.</p>

<PixataGrid Data="Data" Size="_size" Navigable="true" Pageable="true" PageSize="5" Sortable="true" FilterMode="PixataGridFilterMode.FilterMenu" SelectionMode="PixataGridSelectionMode.Multiple">
  <GridColumns>
    <PixataGridColumn Field="@nameof(GridSampleEmployee.FirstName)" />
    <PixataGridColumn Field="@nameof(GridSampleEmployee.Surname)" />
    <PixataGridColumn Field="@nameof(GridSampleEmployee.Pet)" />
    <PixataGridColumn Field="@nameof(GridSampleEmployee.Salary)" DisplayFormat="{0:C0}" />
  </GridColumns>
</PixataGrid>

<h4>Highlighting</h4>

<p>The second and third rows are highlighted with <code>HighlightedItems</code>, and the first row's salary with <code>HighlightedCells</code>.</p>

<PixataGrid Data="Data.Take(5)" Size="_size" HighlightedItems="Data.Skip(1).Take(2)" HighlightedCells="_pixataHighlightedCells">
  <GridColumns>
    <PixataGridColumn Field="@nameof(GridSampleEmployee.FirstName)" />
    <PixataGridColumn Field="@nameof(GridSampleEmployee.Surname)" />
    <PixataGridColumn Field="@nameof(GridSampleEmployee.Salary)" DisplayFormat="{0:C0}" />
  </GridColumns>
</PixataGrid>

<h4>Translation and right to left</h4>

<p>This grid is given Hebrew text through its <code>Messages</code> parameter, and is inside an element with <code>dir="rtl"</code>, so it is laid out from right to left. The first column is frozen, so it sticks on the right when the grid scrolls sideways.</p>

<div dir="rtl">
  <PixataGrid Data="Data" Size="_size" Messages="HebrewMessages" Pageable="true" PageSize="5" Sortable="true" FilterMode="PixataGridFilterMode.FilterRow" Groupable="true" Resizable="true" Width="700px">
    <GridColumns>
      <PixataGridColumn Field="@nameof(GridSampleEmployee.FirstName)" Title="שם פרטי" Width="150px" Locked="true" />
      <PixataGridColumn Field="@nameof(GridSampleEmployee.Surname)" Title="שם משפחה" Width="200px" />
      <PixataGridColumn Field="@nameof(GridSampleEmployee.Pet)" Title="חיית מחמד" Width="200px" />
      <PixataGridColumn Field="@nameof(GridSampleEmployee.Salary)" Title="משכורת" Width="200px" DisplayFormat="{0:C0}" />
    </GridColumns>
  </PixataGrid>
</div>

<h4>Small screens</h4>

<p>With <code>AdaptiveMode="Auto"</code>, on a screen 768px wide or less, the filter menu, column menu and popup editor fill the screen. Make the window narrow, or open the page on a phone, to see it.</p>

<PixataGrid Data="Data" Size="_size" AdaptiveMode="PixataGridAdaptiveMode.Auto" Pageable="true" PageSize="5" Sortable="true" FilterMode="PixataGridFilterMode.FilterMenu" ShowColumnMenu="true">
  <GridColumns>
    <PixataGridColumn Field="@nameof(GridSampleEmployee.FirstName)" />
    <PixataGridColumn Field="@nameof(GridSampleEmployee.Surname)" />
    <PixataGridColumn Field="@nameof(GridSampleEmployee.Salary)" DisplayFormat="{0:C0}" />
  </GridColumns>
</PixataGrid>

<h4>Auto-generated columns</h4>

<p>With <code>AutoGenerateColumns="true"</code> and no <code>GridColumns</code>, there's a column for each simple public property. Phone is left out by <code>[Display(AutoGenerateField = false)]</code>, and Address, being an object, is left out by <code>PixataGrid</code>. The grid has no height, so it is as tall as its rows.</p>

<PixataGrid Data="Data.Take(5)" Size="_size" AutoGenerateColumns="true" />

